Topic 19 – Static and Final Keywords
Objective: Static variables, methods, initialization blocks, final variables, final methods and final classes.
No.	Program	Requirement
01	Static Variable	Create a class with a static variable and access it through the class name.
02	Static Variable Shared	Create multiple objects and modify a static variable. Observe how the value is shared.
03	Static Method	Create a static method and invoke it from the main method and another class.
04	Static and Non-Static	Demonstrate accessing static and non-static members from static and non-static methods.
05	Static Block	Create a class with a static block and main method. Observe the execution sequence.
06	Multiple Static Blocks	Create multiple static blocks and observe their execution order.
07	Final Variable	Declare final variables and demonstrate initialization at declaration and through a constructor.
08	Final Method	Create a parent class with a final method and attempt to override it in a child class. Observe the compiler restriction.
09	Final Class	Create a final class and attempt to extend it. Observe the compiler restriction.
10	Automation Configuration	Create a class containing static final constants for application URL, timeout and test environment values. Access them from another class.